==Enemy==
Big Sal is like an upgraded [[Miss Haka]] - he burrows infinitely until he reaches the [[Cat Base]], and has only one knockback to boot, while also reviving once with 50% health. With Base Destroyer and upwards of 120k attack in most of his appearances, it's effectively guaranteed that he'll destroy the base in one hit if allowed to complete his attack animation. However, he moves very slowly on the battlefield and has short range.

==Strategy==
The traditional strategy to deal with him alone is to mass-produce units with high DPS like [[Titan Cat (Normal Cat)|Jamiera Cat]], [[Crazed Bird Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Crazed UFO Cat]] and [[Crazed Fish Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Crazed Whale Cat]] to inflict as much damage as possible between burrows, and use [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut]] only after he revives to kill him off. Another strategy for a lone Sal is to use [[Freshman Cat Jobs (Super Rare Cat)|Prof. Cat Jobs]], who can weaken his damage to 1%, preventing him from destroying the base easily. In levels such as [[Deep Sea Dying]], however, Big Sal is spawned in hordes, so you'll have to press your luck with the [[Surge Attack|Surge]] created by Prof. Cat Jobs' [[True Form]] or rush the stage before the threats spawn.

Units such as [[Piledriver Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Power Piledriver Cat]], [[Welterweight Cat (Rare Cat)|Heavyweight Cat]], [[Meditation Cat (Special Cat)|Paragon Cat]] and [[Mighty Bomburr (Uber Rare Cat)|NEK-0 Sky Fortress]] can keep Big Sal away from the base with their knockback abilities. NEK-0 Sky Fortress can even solo him, provided if it gets one hit in, meaning that you can't spawn other units or Sal will burrow and cause NEK-0 Sky Fortress to miss its attack.

Stacking any other crowd-controller who can freeze Zombies is another way to deal with Big Sal. [[Gardener Cat (Rare Cat)|Lumbercat]] is one of the best for this job, and when paired with [[Healer (Special Cat)|Healer Cat CC]] in [[The Infected King]], they can easily permafreeze him. Lumbercat might also get the last hit in due to his high attack rate, swiftly finishing him off.

