==Trivia==
*He is a [[wikipedia:Japanese giant salamander|Japanese giant salamander]], the third-largest amphibian in the world. This endangered species has poor eyesight and extremely slow metabolisms, but their skin is covered in special sensory cells that can pick up on vibrations made by their prey. They can also open their mouths very wide, though not as much as Big Sal. His undead nature and Revive ability are an exaggeration of salamanders' regenerative abilities; a colloquialism for the Japanese giant salamander is ''[https://yokai.com/hanzaki/ hanzaki]'', for how it was once believed that they could even survive being cut in half (''han''),
*His Japanese name, Ō-san (オオさん), may be derived from 大山椒魚 ''Ōsanshōuo'' (Japanese giant salamander), 大 ''ō'' (big), おっさん ''ossan'' (a derogatory term for a middle-aged or old man), さん ''-san'' (an honorific roughly equivalent to Mr. or Ms.) and ''[[wikipedia:Sadaharu Oh|Sadaharu Oh]]''. Both Big Sal and Oh are retired baseball players, and the "4-legged batting style" (4本足打法) in Big Sal's Japanese description is a reference to the "flamingo" leg kick or "[[wikipedia:ja:一本足打法|1-legged batting style]]" (1本足打法) that Oh is famous for.
*His spritesheet contains an unused black [[Wave Attack]]-like effect, later used in [[Axoloty]]'s attack animation.
*Prior to [[Version 5.8 Update|Version 5.8]], Big Sal was limited to burrowing 9,999 times.
*In the Spanish translation of the game, Big Sal is named ''Peréz Ozo'', treating him as if he were a [[:Category:Zombie Enemies|Zombie]] variant of [[THE SLOTH]] ''(Peréz Oso).''

